{"causes": ["The historical life of Siddhartha Gautama and his quest for spiritual liberation culminated in his enlightenment at this specific location.", "Emperor Ashoka's patronage in the 3rd century BCE solidified Bodh Gaya's status as a major pilgrimage site by erecting the first temple and a Bodhi Tree sapling.", "The sustained belief in the power of sacred sites and relics within early Buddhist practice encouraged the development and veneration of Bodh Gaya."], "effects": ["Bodh Gaya became the primary pilgrimage destination for Buddhists worldwide, fostering the development of monastic complexes and pilgrimage routes across Asia.", "The architectural styles and iconography developed at Bodh Gaya, particularly the Mahabodhi Temple, influenced Buddhist temple construction across the Indian subcontinent and beyond.", "The continued veneration of Bodh Gaya contributed significantly to the transmission of Buddhist doctrines and practices to various cultures over two millennia."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "siddhartha-gautama", "sourceName": "Siddhartha Gautama", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "bodh-gaya", "targetName": "Bodh Gaya", "context": "Siddhartha Gautama attained enlightenment under the Bodhi Tree in Bodh Gaya around 500 BCE, establishing the site's foundational significance."}, {"sourceSlug": "ashoka-the-great", "sourceName": "Ashoka the Great", "verb": "TRANSFORMS", "targetSlug": "bodh-gaya", "targetName": "Bodh Gaya", "context": "Emperor Ashoka's pilgrimage and construction efforts in the 3rd century BCE transformed Bodh Gaya into a major imperial Buddhist center."}, {"sourceSlug": "mahayan-buddhism", "sourceName": "Mahayana Buddhism", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "bodh-gaya", "targetName": "Bodh Gaya", "context": "The rise of Mahayana Buddhism from the 1st century CE onwards intensified pilgrimage and monastic development at Bodh Gaya, attracting devotees from across Asia."}, {"sourceSlug": "mahabodhi-temple", "sourceName": "Mahabodhi Temple", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "bodh-gaya", "targetName": "Bodh Gaya", "context": "The Mahabodhi Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage site, is the central architectural complex located within Bodh Gaya."}, {"sourceSlug": "buddhist-pilgrimage", "sourceName": "Buddhist Pilgrimage", "verb": "DEFINES", "targetSlug": "bodh-gaya", "targetName": "Bodh Gaya", "context": "Bodh Gaya defines the ultimate destination for Buddhist pilgrimage, being the site of the Buddha's enlightenment, making it a focal point for spiritual journeys."}], "places": [{"name": "Gaya, India", "role": "Nearby District"}, {"name": "Bihar, India", "role": "State Location"}, {"name": "Lumbini, Nepal", "role": "Co-Holy Site"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Bodh Gaya", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "bodh-gaya"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q176767", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodh_Gaya"], "tags": ["India", "human settlement", "Asia", "Cities", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Bodh Gaya contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Served as a center of human activity and development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 8, "significanceNarrative": "Bodh Gaya is globally significant as the site of Gautama Buddha's enlightenment, serving as the spiritual heart of Buddhism and influencing the architectural, artistic, and pilgrimage traditions of a major world religion across Asia for over two millennia. Its enduring status as the paramount Buddhist holy site has shaped the cultural and religious landscape of numerous civilizations.", "significanceCategory": "continental"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-06T21:14:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27074030672", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Bodh Gayā is a religious site and place of pilgrimage associated with the Mahabodhi Temple complex, situated in the Gaya district in the Indian state of Bihar. It is famous for being the place where Gautama Buddha is said to have attained enlightenment under what became known as the Bodhi Tree. Since antiquity, Bodh Gayā has remained the object of pilgrimage and veneration for Buddhists. Archaeological finds, including sculptures, show that the site was in use by Buddhists since the Maurya period. Bodh Gaya is a human settlement in South Asia. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "Bodh Gaya, nestled in the Gaya district of Bihar, India, stands as the paramount pilgrimage site for Buddhists worldwide, revered as the place where Siddhartha Gautama achieved enlightenment (bodhi) under the sacred Bodhi Tree around 500 BCE. This sacred ground, centered around the Mahabodhi Temple complex, defines a spiritual nexus where a prince renounced worldly desires to become the Buddha, thereby establishing one of the world's major religions. Its enduring significance lies in its direct association with the foundational moment of Buddhism, making it a critical geographical and spiritual anchor for over two millennia.

The site's historical development began with Emperor Ashoka's visit in the 3rd century BCE, who is credited with building the first temple or stupa at the spot and planting a sapling from the original Bodhi Tree. The current Mahabodhi Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage site, largely dates from the Gupta period (4th-6th centuries CE), with subsequent renovations and expansions by various dynasties, including the Pala Empire. Key structures include the Vajrasana (Diamond Throne), marking the exact spot of the Buddha's meditation, and numerous stupas and monasteries erected by pilgrims and patrons from across Asia, reflecting centuries of devotion and architectural evolution.

Bodh Gaya's spiritual magnetism has profoundly shaped the trajectory of Buddhist thought, art, and pilgrimage, influencing the spread of Buddhism from India to Southeast Asia, East Asia, and Tibet. Its veneration fostered the creation of pilgrimage routes and the dissemination of Buddhist iconography, architectural styles, and textual traditions across diverse cultures. The site's continued importance as a living pilgrimage center underscores its role in maintaining global Buddhist identity and practice, drawing millions of devotees annually who seek to connect with the Buddha's enlightenment."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-06T21:14:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27074030672", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Geographic and historical development"], "newValue": ["The historical life of Siddhartha Gautama and his quest for spiritual liberation culminated in his enlightenment at this specific location.", "Emperor Ashoka's patronage in the 3rd century BCE solidified Bodh Gaya's status as a major pilgrimage site by erecting the first temple and a Bodhi Tree sapling.", "The sustained belief in the power of sacred sites and relics within early Buddhist practice encouraged the development and veneration of Bodh Gaya."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-06T21:14:29Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#27074030672", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Served as a center of human activity and development"], "newValue": ["Bodh Gaya became the primary pilgrimage destination for Buddhists worldwide, fostering the development of monastic complexes and pilgrimage routes across Asia.", "The architectural styles and iconography developed at Bodh Gaya, particularly the Mahabodhi Temple, influenced Buddhist temple construction across the Indian subcontinent and beyond.", "The continued veneration of Bodh Gaya contributed significantly to the transmission of Buddhist doctrines and practices to various cultures over two millennia."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-06